        "thinking": "OK, wrangler was updated to 4.87.0 (it seems it picked up 4.26.1 for now, let me check). \n\nBut the user also sent a message asking to fix the 501 errors. Let me analyze what they are:\n\n1. `/api/adapters` - adapter routes (uses Node.js)\n2. `/api/companies/:id/events/ws` - WebSocket (real-time events)\n\n\n3. `/api/companies/:id/skills` - company skills\n4. `/api/plugins/ui-contributions` - plugin routes (uses Node.js)\n5. `/api/companies/:id/join-requests` - join requests (in access.ts)\n6. `/api/companies/:id/user-directory` - user directory (in access.ts)\n\nNow I need to figure out which of these can actually run on Cloudflare Workers without Node.js dependencies. The WebSocket endpoint for real-time events is particularly tricky since it would need Durable Objects and a lot of new implementation work.\n\nLooking at the skills endpoint, there's already a CfCompanySkillsService in the CF package, so that seems doable. The join requests and user directory routes both look like straightforward database queries that should work fine. The adapters endpoint won't work because it relies on the file system, and the plugin UI contributions route needs the Node.js plugin worker manager, so those are out.",
